{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/171903-dragon-blooded-demographics-in-creation","id":171903,"title":"Dragon-Blooded demographics in Creation","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-17T12:49:58-07:00","id":171903,"title":"Dragon-Blooded demographics in Creation","content":"Obviously, the Realm is the largest single collection of Terrestrials in the world, with Lookshy as runner-up. What are the next largest groups?<br /> <br /> Is it the Forest Witches? The ruling families of Port Calin? That tribe of Bat Beastmen? Some group you made up?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-17T13:19:04-07:00","id":171942,"title":"","content":"I recall reading somewhere that it's <i>supposed</i> to be the Forest Witches, who would be really dangerous were they to rally behind the cause of a single leader and start looking outward in any serious way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-17T13:21:40-07:00","id":171948,"title":"","content":"Them DBs in the sunken First Age city in the Underworld.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1628-emeraldstreak","name":"emeraldstreak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1628_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-24T15:30:40-07:00","id":179274,"title":"","content":"Last I checked the Forrest Witches had like 8 terrestrials total. The Marmorean Circle beats that with like 12 terrestrials.<br /> <br /> White Wall, Paragon and depending which sources you go by Cherak &amp; Halta all have about 100 Terrestrials or less.<br /> <br /> The Realm had around 10,000 (according to the census that was taken before the Tepet defeat so now much less), Lookshy has about 3,000.<br /> <br /> Every where else is like a dozen or less Terrestrials per area.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-24T16:08:19-07:00","id":179287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/171903-dragon-blooded-demographics-in-creation?p=179274#post179274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Last I checked the Forrest Witches had like 8 terrestrials total.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tom Hanks has witches?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-24T16:39:51-07:00","id":179330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/171903-dragon-blooded-demographics-in-creation?p=179274#post179274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Last I checked the Forrest Witches had like 8 terrestrials total. The Marmorean Circle beats that with like 12 terrestrials.<br /> <br /> White Wall, Paragon and depending which sources you go by Cherak &amp; Halta all have about 100 Terrestrials or less.<br /> <br /> The Realm had around 10,000 (according to the census that was taken before the Tepet defeat so now much less), Lookshy has about 3,000.<br /> <br /> Every where else is like a dozen or less Terrestrials per area.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sunken Clepsys in the Underworld has about 1000.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-24T16:53:17-07:00","id":179335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Realm had around 10,000 (according to the census that was taken before the Tepet defeat so now much less</div> </div> </div> </div> After the last discussion of the whole Tepet legions thing, and rechecking the significantly different House write-up from some First Edition books, not that much less, I think. Maybe a few dozen, probably not much more than sixty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-24T17:00:49-07:00","id":179340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/171903-dragon-blooded-demographics-in-creation?p=179330#post179330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sunken Clepsys in the Underworld has about 1000.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Best place to start Exalted Fallout campaign with players who know nothing of the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1628-emeraldstreak","name":"emeraldstreak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1628_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-24T18:13:04-07:00","id":179398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/171903-dragon-blooded-demographics-in-creation?p=179330#post179330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sunken Clepsys in the Underworld has about 1000.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was just the initial survivors. There could be more now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-24T18:18:11-07:00","id":179400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/171903-dragon-blooded-demographics-in-creation?p=179335#post179335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> After the last discussion of the whole Tepet legions thing, and rechecking the significantly different House write-up from some First Edition books, not that much less, I think. Maybe a few dozen, probably not much more than sixty.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that there were a few other conflicts going on in addition to the Battle of Futile Blood.<br /> <br /> After the Battle of Mishaka, the only reason the ruler of Thorns stayed in power was because the Realm sent in Terrestrials to give his power base a boost, I would say a good chunk of them didn't survive the Mask taking Thorns.<br /> <br /> So if you start taking all the instances of an army getting routed and its Terrestrial commanders being killed or a Wyld Hunt being defeated, etc and add them all together, it is very easy to get into the hundreds of Terrestrials lost in about a 7 year period.<br /> <br /> And just for consideration, Secondary Schools in the Realm take about 7 years. So the Terrestrials who exalted the same year at the census would only now be leaving school and literally graduating to bigger adventures. Thus they would be essence 2 to essence 3 at most.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-24T18:25:13-07:00","id":179405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/171903-dragon-blooded-demographics-in-creation?p=179330#post179330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sunken Clepsys in the Underworld has about 1000.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only about 1,000 people survived the sinking of Saigoth, it is never stated how many of those survivors were Terrestrial, Celestial, Gods, Elementals or just plain mortals. Furthermore we have no information on their current numbers. Though it is conceivable that they would have one of the purer bloodlines, albeit probably death-tainted, at this point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-24T23:41:50-07:00","id":179495,"title":"","content":"Cherak definitely is high up there on the list. Remember, they have several stable dragonblooded family lines in there (named as single house just for convenience), as well as one of major Iselsi households in exile (Enuma). The reason why they are often forgotten is because they are formally part of the Realm.<br /> About Port Calin, i don't remember where i have read that (so it might have been something non-canon), but i remember seeing somewhere that their &quot;genses&quot; are mostly mortal by now, with only a limited number of DB's.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><i>The difference between fiction and reality? Fiction has to make sense.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/434-astralporing","name":"Astralporing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T10:33:29-07:00","id":179840,"title":"","content":"Wasn't there a population of oppressed, second-class DB citizens in Luthe? They should be fairly numerous by now...<br /> <br /> Also, what book did the DB Batfolk tribe show up in? And weren't there some DB People of the Air far to the North?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T13:12:39-07:00","id":179984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/171903-dragon-blooded-demographics-in-creation?p=179840#post179840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasn't there a population of oppressed, second-class DB citizens in Luthe? They should be fairly numerous by now...</div> </div> </div> </div>Um, not quite.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CoTD: The West</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the Traitorspawn have a secret. Four years ago, a Traitorspawn child Exalted as a Water Aspect Dragon-Blood but through luck and quick thinking was able to conceal his Exaltation from his overseers.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing about Luthe is that while there might be bloodlines that could be argued to be of Patrician pedigree, they don't actually have any exalts in the population except for the one plot device character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T13:43:37-07:00","id":180040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/171903-dragon-blooded-demographics-in-creation?p=179274#post179274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Last I checked the Forrest Witches had like 8 terrestrials total. The Marmorean Circle beats that with like 12 terrestrials.</div> </div> </div> </div>87 living Dragon-Blooded and the weirdness of their dead still being considered Terrestrial Exalts thanks to the Sea of Mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T21:42:23-07:00","id":180400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/171903-dragon-blooded-demographics-in-creation?p=179840#post179840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasn't there a population of oppressed, second-class DB citizens in Luthe? They should be fairly numerous by now...</div> </div> </div> </div>It's more a caste of oppressed scapegoats descended from the people who may or may not have descended from people who may or may not have descended from DBs. Any who Exalt as Dragon-Blooded are rounded up and painfully executed, as well as any of them who get in the way or are around when the others feel like punishing somebody. One DB has managed to escape these purges, but that does not a dynasty make. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And weren't there some DB People of the Air far to the North?</div> </div> </div> </div>Unlikely for First Edition, considering they both needed machines to reproduce, and <i>were extinct</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T10:57:22-07:00","id":203970,"title":"","content":"Found what I was looking for in the Wyld Compass: The People of the Air number about 7000 in the far northern city of Sezakan. In addition to the God-Blooded among them, there are about a dozen DBs of Air and Fire aspect ruling in their Solar Council. Similarly, Seahome has more than a dozen DBs among its 6000 People of the Sea. <br /> <br /> Those numbers seem a bit low, esp considering that the Air Folk's Terrestrials descended from &quot;several dozen Dragon-Blooded loyalists&quot; and the Sea Folk have a policy of accepting female Lost Eggs who want to escape the patriarchal atmosphere of the West. I guess they all must have pretty low Breeding traits...<br /> <br /> Also, the tribe of beastmen I mentioned are the Blood Bats, who live in the jungles near Rathess, herding humans whose blood they drink. Interestingly, they have a twisted belief in the Unconquered Sun, that if he is not fed human blood every day, the sun will never set and will burn the world to ashes! So they are always on the hunt for sacrifices...There are an unspecified number of Terrestrials amongst them, who rule all the rest. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T12:14:48-07:00","id":204044,"title":"","content":"Does anyone else think that the Dragonblood demographics make no sense? Even if only one parent is a Dragonblood, there's a 40% chance that any child born will also be a Dragonblood. Further, if both parents are Dragonbloods, even of the worst Breeding, the child has a 60% chance of becoming a Dragonblood. I know that it's 'not safe' for a female Dragonblood to give birth more than once every 5 years or so, but given that 300 is an average lifespan, the population of Dragonbloods in Creation should be exponentially higher than it currently is, especially so given their amorous nature.<br /> <br /> I generally run it that Lookshy has around 15,000 Terrestrials and the Realm 50,000 with the numbers of Outcastes in the hundreds of thousands. Granted, I also number the total population of mortals, godbloods, and dragonbloods at 6 billion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1910,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1910-seconis","user":"Seconis","date":". 07-21-2014, 03:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1910-seconis","name":"Seconis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T13:24:01-07:00","id":204154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/171903-dragon-blooded-demographics-in-creation?p=204044#post204044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if only one parent is a Dragonblood, there's a 40% chance that any child born will also be a Dragonblood. Further, if both parents are Dragonbloods, even of the worst Breeding, the child has a 60% chance of becoming a Dragonblood.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those statistics are calibrated for the sake of stories in general and player characters in particular, they don't reflect the reality of the setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seconis</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know that it's 'not safe' for a female Dragonblood to give birth more than once every 5 years or so, but given that 300 is an average lifespan, the population of Dragonbloods in Creation should be exponentially higher than it currently is</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say that the full length of their lifespan isn't entirely relevant, since I imagine that raising a Dynastic child is so effort intensive that they typically set aside long portions of their lives to dedicate entirely to that matter, and at all other times it's pushed aside. That, combined with the relative expense (not to mention the usual considerations for not having children constantly, combined with the implications of Dragon Blooded power) means that members of the Dynasty aren't really pushing to maximize their number of children in general.<br /> <br /> I'd also say that a not insignificant portion of Dynasts die before they have a chance to sire any children of their own. I mean, their schooling period alone... the House of Bells is a period of military training so intense that it would kill mortals, the Heptagram is four score teenagers all locked up together on an island to learn sorcery (and occasionally get used as guinea pigs by their teachers), and the Spiral Academy is where they go to learn cut-throat business practices and political corruption, I'd say a graduating class without at least three &quot;unexplained&quot; deaths or disappearances is considered a dull affair. Then, upon graduation, they go off to adventure through the dangerous Threshold for years or decades, from which I'd say many never return for the attraction of life free from Dynastic society alone.<br /> <br /> After that, you've got a singificant number who make a life long career of military service, on top of my expectation that any Dynasts who survive to retirement age having devoted some of their time in military endeavors (and a large proportion of the ones who don't make it to retirement age having died doing so).<br /> <br /> If we assume that the average Dynast has twenty children in their lifetime (most have a fair number fewer), I'd say that only maybe half the Dynasty has Breeding good enough for more than half their children to Exalt (with most of the rest being more like a third, with some fairly weak blooded who only get two or three floating around the periphery), and of those children who do Exalt maybe a third die before they have any children of their own, and another third die before they're halfway through their lives.<br /> <br /> If you're a Dynast who lives to retirement age, you've probably outlived all of your siblings, and in the majority of cases where you haven't, their own family lines have been fairly thinned out (which contributes to them being weak enough to not be murdered before they got to retirement). In general, I think Dynast families are a kind of pyramidal structure, where each generation consists of more people than the one above it since they haven't been around long enough to be killed yet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seconis</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">especially so given their amorous nature.</div> </div> </div> </div>Haha hahahaha hahaha no.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seconis</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Granted, I also number the total population of mortals, godbloods, and dragonbloods at 6 billion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where does their food come from?!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T13:58:10-07:00","id":204200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/171903-dragon-blooded-demographics-in-creation?p=204154#post204154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Those statistics are calibrated for the sake of stories in general and player characters in particular, they don't reflect the reality of the setting.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if you disregard what the material has to say on how often a child Exalts, then yeah, I mean, there's no way to say how many Dragonbloods there really should be. Personally, I can't see a reason why the devs would provide statistical information like that if it wasn't supposed to be representative. After all, as an ST, I'm not about to say, &quot;Nope, you sucked at rolling one die and now you have to wait for the next kid to pop in a few years.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/171903-dragon-blooded-demographics-in-creation?p=204154#post204154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd say that the full length of their lifespan isn't entirely relevant, since I imagine that raising a Dynastic child is so effort intensive that they typically set aside long portions of their lives to dedicate entirely to that matter, and at all other times it's pushed aside. That, combined with the relative expense (not to mention the usual considerations for not having children constantly, combined with the implications of Dragon Blooded power) means that members of the Dynasty aren't really pushing to maximize their number of children in general.<br /> <br /> I'd also say that a not insignificant portion of Dynasts die before they have a chance to sire any children of their own. I mean, their schooling period alone... the House of Bells is a period of military training so intense that it would kill mortals, the Heptagram is four score teenagers all locked up together on an island to learn sorcery (and occasionally get used as guinea pigs by their teachers), and the Spiral Academy is where they go to learn cut-throat business practices and political corruption, I'd say a graduating class without at least three &quot;unexplained&quot; deaths or disappearances is considered a dull affair. Then, upon graduation, they go off to adventure through the dangerous Threshold for years or decades, from which I'd say many never return for the attraction of life free from Dynastic society alone.<br /> <br /> After that, you've got a singificant number who make a life long career of military service, on top of my expectation that any Dynasts who survive to retirement age having devoted some of their time in military endeavors (and a large proportion of the ones who don't make it to retirement age having died doing so).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It says throughout the source book for Dragonbloods and on the Blessed Isle that producing children is one of the main goals of any Dynast. I don't disagree that the life of a Dynast is one of mortal peril, luckily, they're not mortal. <br /> <br /> It actually took me a long time to find 'the numbers' on how many Dragonbloods were purported to exist in Creation. Up until then, simply going from all of the other information that you're provided regarding their behavior and their societies, I simply assumed that they numbered in the millions. Sure, Dynast upbringing is an expensive process, but the majority of the Houses desperately seek out Lost Eggs and adopt them all of the time, so it can't be so expensive that it's not worth the cost.<br /> <br /> Regardless of the Dynasts themselves, I'm mostly concerned with the number of Outcastes. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/171903-dragon-blooded-demographics-in-creation?p=204154#post204154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where does their food come from?!<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Creation has more landmass than Earth does. It also has Dragonbloods, Godbloods, and literal Spirits who can create food and increase the fertility of the land manyfold. Further, it's stated that the Blessed Isle has several growing seasons in every year and, as you go further East, the fertility of the land increases exponentially. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1910-seconis","name":"Seconis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T14:09:13-07:00","id":204206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Regardless of the Dynasts themselves, I'm mostly concerned with the number of Outcastes. </div> </div> </div> Even if an Outcaste had Breeding good enough to have more than one Exalted child, at best, I'd say it's super difficult to be one whose children aren't constantly murdered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T21:11:41-07:00","id":204644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/171903-dragon-blooded-demographics-in-creation?p=204044#post204044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone else think that the Dragonblood demographics make no sense?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not just you - they're insane. Better numbers are something on the order of 1-in-5 to 1-in-100 for Dragon-Blooded parents, depending on breeding, with one-in-thousands for unExalted Dynast parents, one-in-hundred-thousands for random peasants, and lower odds from there.<br /> <br /> (Note that the books also can't decide how many Dragon-Blooded children there are - implying in some places that there are hundreds of school-age DBs, which suggests a mortality rate worse than some warzones. A more plausible number is ~20 future-DBs born to the Realm every year.)<br /> <br /> (I had some statistical models that made this all work, but then the old forum went away.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}